feat(transparency): public AI receipt page — Trust Director's #3 mandate

When Cristian's AI drafts a customer-facing message, the recipient
should be able to verify what the AI knew. ServiceTitan/Jobber/Housecall
don't ship this — their AI features can't cite a source. We can,
because every Ask Gladius and Quote Drafter call writes an `ai_run` row
from day one (audit chain shipped 2026-05-07).

What landed:
- New /receipt/[id] route — public, anonymous-readable, server-rendered.
  Looks up the ai_run row by UUID; renders surface (Ask Gladius / Quote
  Drafter) + timestamp + model + prompt fingerprint (sha256, 32 chars) +
  output excerpt (first 600 chars) + the "why this exists" disclosure +
  link to /legal/dpa + /legal/privacy.
- Discoverability: UUIDs are unguessable. The link is generated by the
  AI surface (Quote Drafter footer, Concierge SMS) and shipped with the
  message. Anyone WITH the URL can verify; anyone WITHOUT it cannot
  enumerate.
- Restricted column projection — the page never queries the prompt
  body, only the fingerprint. Prompt rotation maps to fingerprint
  changes, which we can confirm to recipients on request.

/app/trust gains a "Show last 5 calls with shareable receipt URLs"
expander on the AI Runs panel. Each row links to /receipt/[id] in a new
tab. Operator can copy a URL into any AI-drafted message they send.

